WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:10.010
Nowadays, cultivating independent learning ability is becoming increasingly crucial for personal development.
如今，培养自主学习能力对个人发展正变得越来越重要。

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:17.760
In an age when knowledge is updated at an astonishing speed, what we learn at school can hardly meet all our needs in life.
在一个知识以惊人速度更新的时代，我们在学校学到的东西很难满足我们生活中的所有需要。

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.580
Independent learning ability brings many benefits.
自主学习能力带来许多好处。

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.000
First, it enables us to keep up with the times.
第一，它使我们能够跟上时代。

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:32.820
Whenever we face a new field or a new technology, we can find the right materials, make a plan and master it on our own.
每当我们面对一个新领域或一项新技术时，我们都能找到合适的资料，制订计划，然后自己掌握它。

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.870
Second, it fosters critical thinking.
第二，它能培养批判性思维。

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:44.550
Instead of passively accepting what teachers say, independent learners ask questions, compare different views and form their own judgments.
自主学习者不是被动地接受老师所说的一切，而是会提出问题，比较不同的观点，形成自己的判断。

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.990
Third, it builds confidence.
第三，它能增强自信。

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:55.520
Many working adults, for example, have taught themselves programming through online courses and successfully changed careers.
例如，许多在职成年人通过网络课程自学编程，并成功转行。

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.690
Such experiences convince people that they can learn almost anything they set their minds to.
这样的经历使人们相信，几乎任何他们下定决心要学的东西，他们都能学会。

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:10.230
To cultivate this ability, students should learn to set their own goals, manage their time and reflect on their progress regularly.
为了培养这种能力，学生应该学会自己设定目标、管理时间，并定期反思自己的进步。

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:17.870
Teachers should guide their students rather than spoon-feed them, leaving them room to explore and make discoveries of their own.
教师应该引导学生，而不是对他们填鸭式地灌输，给他们留出自己去探索和发现的空间。

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:23.330
With the ability to learn independently, we can keep growing throughout our lives.
有了自主学习的能力，我们就能终其一生不断成长。
